# Competency question (native gmeow:reasoningLogic lane): "Does the DERIVED
# gmeow:gmnRingWithin order, computed by gmeow:ruleGmnRingWithinDerive /
# gmeow:ruleGmnRingCompartmentGap from the three default-preset rings' AUTHORED
# (gmeow:gmnRingLevel, gmeow:gmnRingCompartment) coordinates, reproduce the
# retired hand-chained core-within-trusted-within-restricted edge set?"  The
# FILTER(?x IN (...)) / FILTER(?y IN (...)) pair restricts both variables to
# the three gmeow:gmnRingPresetDefault members so gmeow:gmnRingNato (a fourth,
# differently-compartmented ring at the trusted level) does not contaminate the
# row set. gmeow:gmnRingWithin is REFLEXIVE by construction (a ring is
# trivially within itself, the standard Denning ⊑ reading — see the property's
# skos:definition); FILTER(?x != ?y) excludes those trivial self-pairs so the
# comparison is against the retired chain's STRICT edges, where irreflexivity
# is the property actually being witnessed. Nothing asserts gmeow:gmnRingWithin
# anywhere in the source graph (a separate structural gate enforces that);
# every row here exists only because the derivation fired.
PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>

SELECT ?x ?y WHERE {
    ?x gmeow:gmnRingWithin ?y .
    FILTER(?x IN (gmeow:gmnRingCore, gmeow:gmnRingTrusted, gmeow:gmnRingRestricted))
    FILTER(?y IN (gmeow:gmnRingCore, gmeow:gmnRingTrusted, gmeow:gmnRingRestricted))
    FILTER(?x != ?y)
}
ORDER BY ?x ?y
